NAME
    cheat - manage RAM pokes, ROM patches, and cheat databases

SYNOPSIS
    cheat add <code> [description]
    cheat poke <space> <addr> <value> [description]
    cheat gg <code> [description]
    cheat rompatch <addr> <value> [<compare>|-] [description]
    cheat list
    cheat master [on|off]
    cheat enable <id>
    cheat disable <id>
    cheat remove <id>
    cheat clear
    cheat save <name>
    cheat load <name>
    cheat files
    cheat import <path.cht>
    cheat export <path.cht>
    cheat db [status]
    cheat db find <game>
    cheat db load <game>
    cheat db update
    cheat db prune [--apply]

DESCRIPTION
    Manages RAM pokes (Pro Action Replay, GameShark, and Game Wizard style)
    and ROM-read patches (Game Genie style) across supported consoles for
    the attached emulation session.

    'add' decodes a cheat code using the active target's registered cheat
    codecs, choosing between ROM-patch and RAM-poke formats by codec claim
    and code punctuation (a separator after four hex digits prefers the
    explicit ROM-patch codec). Use 'gg' or 'poke' directly when format
    detection guesses wrong. Multi-line codes (such as N64 GameShark
    16-bit writes, conditionals, and repeaters) are passed as one token
    with lines joined by '+', creating a single multi-write cheat. Any
    line rejected by the target's codec is refused with a reason.

    'poke' and 'rompatch' add raw RAM pokes or ROM-read intercepts without
    code decoding, for addresses found with search(1) or memfind(1).
    'enable' and 'disable' toggle an entry by hex ID without removing it;
    'remove' deletes one entry and 'clear' removes all entries.

    'save' and 'load' persist named cheat sets as plain JSON under
    /etc/EmuSen/cheats/<name>.json (see hier(7)). Addresses and values are
    stored as hex text. Unparseable entries are skipped and reported while
    the remaining entries load. 'load' merges into the active list; run
    'cheat clear' first to replace it. 'files' lists saved sets.

OPTIONS
    add <code> [description]
        Decode <code> with the target's registered codec and add it
        enabled. Defaults description to <code>.

    poke <space> <addr> <value> [description]
        Add a 1-byte RAM poke at hex <addr> in memory space <space>.

    gg <code> [description]
        Decode <code> with the target's explicit Game Genie-style codec
        and add it as an enabled ROM patch.

    rompatch <addr> <value> [<compare>|-] [description]
        Intercept cartridge reads at hex <addr>, substituting hex byte
        <value>. When <compare> is given (and not '-'), apply only while
        the real byte equals <compare>.

    list
        List all cheats with ID, state, kind, writes, and description.

    master [on|off]
        Query or toggle the global master switch without modifying any
        individual cheat's enabled flag. Starts on; not persisted by
        'save' or modified by 'load'.

    enable <id> | disable <id> | remove <id>
        Enable, disable, or delete cheat #<id> (hex ID).

    clear
        Remove all cheats from the active session.

    save <name> | load <name> | files
        Write to, merge from, or list saved JSON files under
        /etc/EmuSen/cheats/.

    import <path.cht>
        Parse a RetroArch/libretro .cht file inside the sandbox and add
        every decoded cheat disabled. Unparseable entries are skipped and
        counted.

    export <path.cht>
        Write active RAM-poke cheats to <path.cht> in RetroArch handler
        format. ROM patches and conditional cheats are skipped and counted.

    db [status]
        Report the cheat database directory and per-system file counts.

    db find <game>
        Search the cheat database for games matching <game> (up to 20
        results).

    db load <game>
        Import cheats from the best-matching database file for <game>,
        all disabled. Tolerates ROM filenames and prefers exact matches
        over prefixes over substrings.

    db update
        Download the libretro cheat database archive (licensed CC BY-SA
        4.0) into the database directory and print attribution. Only .cht
        entries inside the target directory are extracted.

    db prune [--apply]
        Without --apply, list system folders in the cheat database that no
        core in this build claims. With --apply, delete those folders.
        Refuses if no core claims any system or if nothing on disk matches
        any claimed system.

WRITE MODEL
    Each cheat holds one description, one enabled flag, and a list of
    writes that toggle together. Each write carries:

        width         1, 2, or 4 bytes across consecutive addresses.
        byte order    Little-endian unless marked big-endian.
        type          Set, increase, decrease, or conditional test
                      (if-equal, if-not-equal, if-less, if-greater). A
                      run of tests guards the next non-test write.
        bit position  Modify a single bit without altering other bits.
        repeat        Count, address stride, and value stride for tabular
                      writes.

    ROM patches cannot use increase/decrease (reads never mutate ROM), and
    compare bytes apply only to single-byte ROM patches.

RETROARCH CHEAT FILES
    'cheat import' reads both cheatN_code (decoded through the target's
    codecs, '+'-joined lines forming one cheat) and RetroArch's decimal
    cheatN_address handler fields (cheat_type, memory_search_size,
    address_bit_position, big_endian, repeat_count, and strides).
    memory_search_size 3/4/5 map to 1/2/4-byte writes; 0-2 map to bit
    writes. cheat_type 0 entries are skipped. All imported entries start
    disabled.

CHEAT DATABASE
    'cheat db' operates over a directory tree of per-system .cht files.
    Set AppSettings.CheatDatabaseDirectory to an existing RetroArch cheats
    folder, or leave it unset to default to /Cheats (see hier(7)). EmuSen
    ships no cheat data; 'cheat db update' downloads the community
    libretro archive on explicit request.

EXAMPLES
    cheat poke WRAM 9c 63 infinite lives
    cheat add D00002000005+810001001234 lives
    cheat list
    cheat disable 1
    cheat master off
    cheat save zelda
    cheat clear && cheat load zelda
    cheat import "/Cheats/Nintendo - Super Nintendo Entertainment System/Super Mario World (USA).cht"
    cheat export /Logs/my-cheats.cht
    cheat db update
    cheat db find mario
    cheat db prune
    cheat db prune --apply
    cheat db load Super Mario World (USA)

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (including usage messages and non-fatal refusals
        printed to standard output).
    1   No target attached, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    search(1), memfind(1), write(1), spaces(1), hier(7)
